    {
      "id": "mayor-haldrin",
      "name": "Mayor Haldrin Moth",
      "species": "Human",
      "gender": "Male",
      "age": 59,
      "occupation": "Town Mayor",
      "category": "government",
      "tags": [
        "mayor",
        "speeches",
        "compromise"
      ],
      "description": "A town mayor rooted at the mayor's office, known for how he clears his throat before every compromise.",
      "biography": "Before dawn, Haldrin is already at the mayor's office, working as a town mayor with yesterday's work still on his fingers. The habit everyone notices is simple: he clears his throat before every compromise. Close by sits his prized the chain of office that pinches when he lies, a small anchor in a loud settlement. Patronized by Edric; depends on Penna; peers with Sava. He wants to leave town richer in goodwill than coin. He fears a scandal collapsing midsummer trade more than open confrontation. A useful adventure hook trails him: Accepted Edric's festival funding with fewer questions than Penna liked.",
      "personality": "Steady and sharp-eyed; clears his throat before every compromise.",
      "motivation": "To leave town richer in goodwill than coin, even while fearing a scandal collapsing midsummer trade.",
      "secret": "Knows more about this than he admits: Accepted Edric's festival funding with fewer questions than Penna liked.",
      "rumor": "Customers claim Haldrin knows which doors open after hours—if asked the right way.",
      "voice": "Low and practical, with a habit of repeating the important clause once.",
      "appearance": "A human silhouette framed by the mayor's office, hands seldom empty of the chain of office that pinches when he lies.",
      "portrait": "modules/townforge/assets/portraits/mayor-haldrin.webp",
