    {
      "id": "taxer-miln",
      "name": "Miln Tallcount",
      "species": "Halfling",
      "gender": "Male",
      "age": 53,
      "occupation": "Tax Assessor",
      "category": "government",
      "tags": [
        "taxes",
        "math",
        "unpopular"
      ],
      "description": "Miln holds down ledgers and warehouse doors with callused competence and open ears.",
      "biography": "Miln Tallcount's reputation as a tax assessor was built one careful errand at a time around ledgers and warehouse doors. Age 53 sits lightly on this Halfling, except when old debts creak. Watch long enough and you will see that he apologizes and assesses in the same breath. The folding abacus and a rainproof satchel is part tool, part talisman. Unpopular; useful against Nedda; supports Bera. He would trade sleep to fund Bera's second well through honest tallies, yet stays wary of being drowned in a well 'accident' of popularity. Current spark: Found undeclared barge income patterns matching Nedda's trips.",
      "personality": "Warm with regulars, curt with wasters; apologizes and assesses in the same breath.",
      "motivation": "Secure enough ground to fund Bera's second well through honest tallies.",
      "secret": "Quietly arranging matters around this problem: Found undeclared barge income patterns matching Nedda's trips.",
      "rumor": "Customers claim Miln knows which doors open after hours—if asked the right way.",
      "voice": "Polite public voice; sharper private asides when trust appears.",
