    {
      "id": "judge-sava",
      "name": "Judge Sava Wren",
      "species": "Half-Elf",
      "gender": "Female",
      "age": 61,
      "occupation": "Magistrate",
      "category": "government",
      "tags": [
        "judge",
        "fair",
        "law"
      ],
      "description": "Local magistrate whose days orbit a modest courtroom and small lasting loyalties.",
      "biography": "Judge Sava Wren works from a modest courtroom with the stubborn patience of a 61-year-old Half-Elf who has already survived harder seasons. She makes eye contact with the poorest person first, and keeps the gavel with a softened rim close when tempers rise. Peer to Mayor; works with Crowe and Merrick. Her private aim is simple: set a precedent that ledgers bind lords too. Still, she flinches at the thought of nobles buying outcomes through festival gifts. Lately a fresh problem has landed in her lap: Asked Merrick for a clean chain of evidence on Rook before festival court.",
      "personality": "Dry humor over a careful heart; makes eye contact with the poorest person first.",
      "motivation": "Finish one honest plan: set a precedent that ledgers bind lords too.",
      "secret": "Keeps proof related to a problem—Asked Merrick for a clean chain of evidence on Rook before festival court.",
      "rumor": "Locals whisper that the gavel with a softened rim once belonged to a traveler who vanished on the road.",
      "voice": "Storyteller rhythm even when discussing ledgers or latches.",
      "appearance": "Half-Elf features shaped by work at a modest courtroom; watch for the gavel with a softened rim.",
      "portrait": "modules/townforge/assets/portraits/judge-sava.webp",
