      "description": "Bol holds down the public square with callused competence and open ears.",
      "biography": "Before dawn, Bol is already at the public square, working as a town herald with yesterday's work still on his fingers. The habit everyone notices is simple: he projects news until windows open. Close by sits his prized the brass bell with a cracked throat, a small anchor in a loud settlement. Voice of government; confused by mill intrigue. He wants to be trusted with truth, not only volume. He fears reading a proclamation that starts a riot more than open confrontation. A useful adventure hook trails him: Was handed two conflicting proclamations about mill ownership in one morning.",
